      "writtenOn": "2017-07-04T22:10:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually it consumes different message (ImageUpdateReq vs. DownloadImage) from RequestSoftwareDownload(now renamed to DownloadImage). It is symmetrical to ActivateSoftwareUpdate.\n\nActivateImageUpdate: activates the specified software from standby partition to active partition. \n\nRevertImageUpdate: deactivates and specified image from active partition, and revert to previous image at standby partition.\n\nFor both of those rpc calls, Depending on the device implementation, this call may or may not cause device reboot. If no reboot, the a reboot_device is required to make the image running.\n\nI will add those to inline comments",
